activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T05:15:28.3582702Z {"title": "Memory: 367.6 MB Floating point exception (core dumped)", "body": "### What happens?\n\nBetween `1.4.4` and `1.5.2` a script I use started failing with:\n\n```\nMemory: 367.6 MBFloating point exception (core dumped)\n```\n\n### To Reproduce\n\nCan't post source DB, but it uses a `postgres_attach` and looks like this:\n\n```sql\n\nPRAGMA temp_directory='/tmp/dump-legacy.duck.db';\n.print creating tables\n\nCREATE TABLE table1 ();\nCREATE TABLE table2 ();\n\n.print connect to Postgres DB\n\nINSTALL postgres;\nLOAD postgres;\n\nCALL postgres_attach(\n    concat('host=', getenv('PGHOST'),\n    ' dbname=', getenv('PGDATABASE'),\n    ' user=',  getenv('PGUSER'),\n    ' password=', getenv('PGPASSWORD'))\n    );\n\n.timer on\n\nINSERT INTO table1 (...)\n    SELECT  ... FROM \"PostgresTable1\";\n\nINSERT INTO table2 (...)\n    SELECT  ... FROM \"PostgresTable2\";\n```\n\nIt successfully completes a few tables, then consistently fails on the same one.\n\n### OS:\n\nUbuntu 20.04.4\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.2\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nCLI\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nDave Tapley\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nJE Fuller\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [ ] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNo - I cannot share the data sets because they are confidential"}
